NDEX:The Nutritional Risk Index (NRI) is a tool designed to assess nutritional risk, particularly in elderly patients. It has been associated with perioperative mortality, highlighting its importance in evaluating the nutritional status of individuals who may be at risk during surgical procedures.", "NUFFE:NUFFE, or Nutritional Form For The Elderly, is a specialized tool created to evaluate and assess the nutritional status and needs of elderly patients. It serves as an important resource in understanding the dietary requirements of this demographic, ensuring that their nutritional health is adequately monitored and addressed.", "SKIPER:Skiper is a researcher who has established a grading system for nutritional screening tools based on the quality of studies.", "ELIA:Elia is a researcher who discusses the effectiveness of age as a predictor of mortality and hospital stay compared to nutritional screening tools.", "STRATTON:Stratton is a researcher who has made significant contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly concerning elderly patients. He analyzed various studies on supplementation in older adults and concluded that such interventions have positive effects on nutritional evolution and mortality rates. Additionally, Stratton has contributed to the discourse on the effectiveness of nutritional screening tools for elderly patients, emphasizing the importance of proper assessment in this demographic. He is also the author of a systematic review and meta-analysis published in 2013, which focused on the use of oral supplements following hospital discharge, further highlighting his commitment to improving nutritional outcomes for older individuals.", "CHANDRA NUTRITION SCREEN:The Chandra Nutrition Screen is a tool specifically designed to assess nutritional risk in elderly patients and populations. It aims to identify individuals who may be at risk of malnutrition, thereby facilitating timely interventions to improve their nutritional status and overall health.", "VAN BOKHORST-DE VAN DER SCHUEREN:Van Bokhorst-de van der Schueren is a researcher and author who has published a review on nutritional assessment tools specifically designed for hospitalized elderly patients. This work contributes to the understanding and improvement of nutritional care for this vulnerable population.", "NUTRITION SCREENING INITIATIVE:The Nutrition Screening Initiative is a program designed to enhance the nutritional health of older adults by implementing screening and intervention strategies.", "VGS:The VGS, or Global Subjective Assessment, is a comprehensive tool designed to evaluate the nutritional status of patients, particularly in hospital settings. Developed by Baker in the 1980s, it is recognized as a classic method for assessing the nutritional needs of patients undergoing gastrointestinal surgery. The VGS has been shown to have a high level of agreement with other nutritional assessment tools, making it a reliable choice for healthcare professionals. Additionally, the Visual Geriatric Scale, which is also referred to as VGS, specifically targets the nutritional assessment of hospitalized elderly patients. The VGS is recommended by the American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (ASPEN) as a valuable nutritional screening tool, further emphasizing its importance in clinical practice.", "PCR:PCR, or C-reactive protein, is a significant marker of inflammation that plays a crucial role in evaluating the health status of patients, particularly in surgical contexts. It is commonly used in hospitals to assess the inflammatory status of patients while also considering nutritional parameters. Elevated levels of PCR in laboratory results can indicate a heightened inflammatory response, which may suggest nutritional risk among surgical patients. As a blood test, PCR measures inflammation in the body and is utilized to assess various health conditions, making it an important tool in clinical settings.", "PARAMETROS ANTROPOMETRICOS:PARAMETROS ANTROPOMETRICOS refer to anthropometric parameters, which are measurements utilized to assess the body composition and nutritional status of patients. These parameters play a crucial role in evaluating an individual's health and can provide valuable insights into their physical condition.", "PARAMETROS BIOQUIMICOS:Biochemical parameters are laboratory tests used to evaluate the nutritional status and health of patients.", "EUROPEAN CONSENSUS:The European Consensus is a comprehensive framework that outlines definitions and classifications of sarcopenia, distinguishing between its primary and secondary causes. It provides essential guidelines for diagnosing sarcopenia, particularly in frail patients, with a strong emphasis on the measurement of handgrip strength as a key diagnostic tool. The Consensus highlights the association of sarcopenia with frailty in older adults and underscores the importance of assessing muscle mass and strength in the diagnosis and management of this condition. Additionally, the European Consensus offers guidelines for dietary assessments and monitoring in patients suffering from chronic respiratory diseases, such as cystic fibrosis, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (EPOC), and bronchiectasis (BQ). It serves as a valuable resource for a group of experts who provide recommendations for managing various health conditions, including osteoporosis in patients with cystic fibrosis."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}